phase P4
title Core
description
    Class: verifiable.
    Kind: feature.
    Goal: the production runtime for what the prototypes proved, in `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`,
    built from the core Specs with the prototype open beside it, one module at a time: Compiled
    and the compiler; lane, step and turn; the persistence edge, write-ahead and the driver;
    restore and key versions; fragments; operations; the CLI's `check`, `explain` and `graph`.
    Starts when: P3's completion audit passes (its suite is proven).
    Verified by: P3's suite through a production adapter (coverage record in @plan.Runtime);
    skill:check-task per Task; `nub run check` at zero; `nub run verify`.
    One iteration: the next ready Task: build it against its Spec, check it independently,
    repair. The Pay path first, end to end, as the walking skeleton.
    Exit criteria: the suite passes on the production runtime alone, the prototype adapter
    retired; every gate fails on its broken runtime; `nub run verify` passes; the completion
    audit passes.
    False pass: the production adapter doing work the runtime should. Caught by: mutants run
    against the production adapter, and a review section on the adapter's role.
    Gates: falsify on the production adapter; one probe file per lint rule that `nub run check`
    must reject (`tools/lint-bomb/`).
    Budget: the Epic's Budget section, row P4.
    Failure limit: 2.
    Stops: public entry-point names; a large public API change; a guarantee that can't be met;
    a guarantee change. User's read: the internal module layout; small public API calls.
    Draws from: skill:playbook-build (long runs); skill:execute-task; skill:check-task;
    skill:to-design per module; skill:review; skill:diagnose when a case fails unexplained.
